      You're looking in the wrong place.  That was not a crash,
it was a panic.  NetHack should have created a panic save file
in the save subdirectory instead of leaving the assorted level
files in the game directory.  That simply needs to be renamed
in order to turn it into an ordinary save file, although its
contents might not work reliably depending upon the extent of
the problem which triggered the panic.

      There should also be an entry in the paniclog file which
contains an accurate copy of the message given at the time.
I don't recognize the decribed behavior as a known problem.
The list of fixes has gotten pretty long but there are only 3
panics explicitly listed.  This isn't any of those three, but
might be covered by some less precise entry.


